      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Introduction\r\nOverview: AudioAlchemyLab is a comprehensive audio management
    tool designed to streamline your workflow within Unity. Whether you\u2019re managing
    a small set of sound effects or a large library of music tracks, AudioAlchemyLab
    provides powerful features that allow for effortless playback, intuitive controls,
    and advanced audio management\u2014all directly within the Unity Editor.\r\nKey
    Features:\r\n    \u2022 One-click audio playback\r\n    \u2022 Intuitive interface\r\n   
    \u2022 Advanced volume and pitch control\r\n    \u2022 Simple looping options\r\n   
    \u2022 Play On Awake functionality\r\n    \u2022 Automatic audio source assignment\r\n   
    \u2022 Folder-specific audio loading\r\n    \u2022 Seamless navigation to audio
    files in your project\r\n2. Getting Started\r\nInstallation:\r\n    1. Download
    the AudioAlchemyLab package from the Unity Asset Store\r\n    2. Open your Unity
    project and navigate to Assets > Import Package > Custom Package....\r\n    3.
    Select the AudioAlchemyLab package you downloaded and click \"Import\".\r\nInitial
    Setup:\r\n    1. After importing, open the AudioAlchemyLab window by navigating
    to Tools > Audio Alchemy Lab.\r\n    2. Set your preferred settings in the AudioAlchemyLab
    window. You can adjust things like volume, pitch, and loop settings according
    to your needs.\r\n    3. To start using the tool, simply click on any audio clip
    within the Unity Editor, and AudioAlchemyLab will automatically load it into
    the interface.\r\n3. Features and Usage\r\nEffortless Audio Playback:\r\n   
    \u2022 Play any audio file in your project with a single click. Simply select
    the file in AudioAlchemyLab and press the play button. No need to manually assign
    audio sources.\r\nIntuitive Interface:\r\n    \u2022 The interface is designed
    to be user-friendly, integrating seamlessly into the Unity Editor. It offers
    a clean layout where you can easily navigate and manage your audio assets.\r\nAdvanced
    Control:\r\n    \u2022 Fine-tune the volume and pitch of your audio clips directly
    within the tool. Adjustments are immediately reflected, allowing for precise
    control over how your audio sounds.\r\nLooping Made Simple:\r\n    \u2022 Toggle
    looping for any audio clip with just one click. You can also customize the delay
    between loops to fit your needs.\r\nPlay On Awake:\r\n    \u2022 Easily enable
    or disable the Play On Awake feature for quick audio testing within your scenes.\r\nAuto-Assignment:\r\n   
    \u2022 When you click on an audio clip, AudioAlchemyLab automatically assigns
    it to the selected audio source. This streamlines the process of managing sound
    effects and background music in your project.\r\nFolder Functionality:\r\n   
    \u2022 Load all audio files from any folder within your Assets directory instantly.
    This makes it easy to organize and manage large audio libraries by narrowing
    down your selection to specific folders.\r\nOne-Click Access:\r\n    \u2022 Quickly
    navigate to any audio file in your project with a single click. This feature
    simplifies file management and helps you keep track of where your assets are
    stored.\r\n4. Compatibility and Requirements\r\nSupported Unity Versions:\r\n   
    \u2022 AudioAlchemyLab is compatible with Unity version 2022.3.22f1 and above.\r\nDependencies:\r\n   
    \u2022 This tool does not require any additional packages or plugins. It\u2019s
    designed to work out-of-the-box with your Unity projects.\r\n5. FAQ/Troubleshooting\r\nCommon
    Issues and Solutions:\r\n    \u2022 Issue: AudioAlchemyLab isn\u2019t displaying
    audio files in my project.\r\n        \u25E6 Solution: Ensure that the audio
    files are placed within the Assets directory of your Unity project. The tool
    only scans the Assets folder for audio files.\r\n    \u2022 Issue: The Play On
    Awake feature isn\u2019t working as expected.\r\n        \u25E6 Solution: Double-check
    that the audio source in your scene has the Play On Awake option enabled. Also,
    ensure that the correct audio clip is assigned to the audio source.\r\n    \u2022
    Issue: The looping feature isn\u2019t looping the audio as expected.\r\n       
    \u25E6 Solution: Verify that the loop delay setting is correctly configured in
    AudioAlchemyLab. If the issue persists, try resetting the loop settings to their
    defaults.\r\n6. Changelog\r\nVersion 5.2:\r\n    \u2022 Complete rebuild from
    the ground up.\r\n    \u2022 Added Play On Awake functionality.\r\n    \u2022
    Automatic loading of audio files from the Assets folder.\r\n    \u2022 GUI redesign
    with improved UI scaling.\r\n    \u2022 Data persistence across editor sessions
    and play modes.\r\n    \u2022 Audio Source detection and management.\r\n    \u2022
    Audio clip file management and assignment.\r\n    \u2022 Bug fixes.\r\nVersion
    4.0:\r\n    \u2022 Search functionality fixed.\r\n    \u2022 Major visual and
    UI improvements.\r\n7. Credits and Acknowledgments\r\nContributors:\r\n    \u2022
    The development of AudioAlchemyLab was led by [Tyler Bernard/Reptilian Alien
    Games].\r\nAI Involvement:\r\n    \u2022 This asset\u2019s creation benefited
    from AI technology, particularly ChatGPT, in multiple facets of development.
    ChatGPT provided valuable assistance by generating code snippets, documentation,
    project planning, and contributing to bug fixing efforts. This AI-powered collaboration
    enhanced the asset's development efficiency, quality, and functionality.\r\n\r\nOverview
    Video:\r\n    \u2022 \nSupport Discord:\r\n    \u2022 "
